From: j7
Subject: j7: two pixels per bus read, and paint once per source pixel

The wallpaper paints now (1.4 M pixels in one frame) and the build is still 70 ms of a 78 ms
present, so the cost is not the paint: the client's surface is cache-inhibited and a
3000-byte row cost 47 us, which is one bus transaction per 32-bit load.  Load two pixels at a
time, four loads in flight, and keep memcpy only for a row that is not 8-byte aligned.

The picture decision also ran per output pixel with the picture's column looked up in a
750-entry table per 1080-pixel row.  Do it once per source pixel in the staged row instead,
where the column of the picture is a table built once per present, and let the expansion
loop only copy values.  A new src_us in the copy split line says how much of build_us is the
row read.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

